# tally 2.1.8 S6 (#177), L §8.1 HOLE-SAME: the rows in the order of their ids (L §2.5), whatever order the same line
# writes them in: same zeta = alpha names alpha first, from either side. Reopens P51, which took the written order.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input zeta: money PLN
input alpha: money PLN

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  zeta = 10.00 PLN "s"
  alpha = 12.00 PLN "s"
  same zeta = alpha

ask z: zeta
ask a: alpha
=== expect
a: ?"alpha and zeta are one, but the value differs on every day: 12.00 PLN (v:alpha) and 10.00 PLN (v:zeta)" (alpha, zeta)
  cut 2026-03-01
z: ?"alpha and zeta are one, but the value differs on every day: 12.00 PLN (v:alpha) and 10.00 PLN (v:zeta)" (alpha, zeta)
  cut 2026-03-01
